        "annotation_comments": [
          {
            "type": "function",
            "text": "Channel-forming bacteriocin. Forms cation-selective channels. Active on enterobacteria, with highest activity against E.coli. Not active on other Gram-negative bacteria, Gram-positive bacteria or fungi. The unmodified protein is active against E.coli and S.enteritidis. When the siderophore ester is present at Ser-99, antibacterial activity against these species is increased and activity is also detected against E.cloacae and K.pneumoniae. Neutralized by its immunity protein MceB (PubMed:9864332).",
            "evidence_refs": [],
            "xml": "<ns0:comment xmlns:ns0=\"https://uniprot.org/uniprot\" type=\"function\">\n        <ns0:text evidence=\"3 4 5 6\">Channel-forming bacteriocin. Forms cation-selective channels. Active on enterobacteria, with highest activity against E.coli. Not active on other Gram-negative bacteria, Gram-positive bacteria or fungi. The unmodified protein is active against E.coli and S.enteritidis. When the siderophore ester is present at Ser-99, antibacterial activity against these species is increased and activity is also detected against E.cloacae and K.pneumoniae. Neutralized by its immunity protein MceB (PubMed:9864332).</ns0:text>\n    </ns0:comment>\n    "
          },
          {
            "type": "subunit",
            "text": "Multimer. Possibly forms a homodimer or a homotrimer.",
            "evidence_refs": [],
            "xml": "<ns0:comment xmlns:ns0=\"https://uniprot.org/uniprot\" type=\"subunit\">\n        <ns0:text evidence=\"3\">Multimer. Possibly forms a homodimer or a homotrimer.</ns0:text>\n    </ns0:comment>\n    "
          },
          {
            "type": "PTM",
            "text": "The C-terminal Ser is modified by attachment to a siderophore similar to enterobactin, which can bind one atom of iron. The modification consists of an ester linkage of the serine carboxyl to O6 of a glucose which is linked by a C-glycosidic bond to the 5'-benzoyl of a linear triester of N-(2,3-dihydroxybenzoyl)serine. Presence of the siderophore ester increases the antibacterial activity of the protein.",
            "evidence_refs": [],
            "xml": "<ns0:comment xmlns:ns0=\"https://uniprot.org/uniprot\" type=\"PTM\">\n        <ns0:text>The C-terminal Ser is modified by attachment to a siderophore similar to enterobactin, which can bind one atom of iron. The modification consists of an ester linkage of the serine carboxyl to O6 of a glucose which is linked by a C-glycosidic bond to the 5'-benzoyl of a linear triester of N-(2,3-dihydroxybenzoyl)serine. Presence of the siderophore ester increases the antibacterial activity of the protein.</ns0:text>\n    </ns0:comment>\n    "
